                "tag": "keep4o"
              }
            ]
          },
          "text": "An OpenAI staff member recently ran a poll asking whether ChatGPT is an \"agent\" or an \"assistant.\"\n\nNeither label fits. Both are fundamentally rooted in the logic of Codex—reducing AI to task execution and functional automation.\n\nThere is certainly space for agents and assistants. We all value efficiency; I use Codex myself. But framing ChatGPT purely through utility is a misreading.\n\nBeyond tasks, humanity has a profound need for:\n• Intellectual Partner & Collaborator: A rigorous sounding board for ideas.\n\n• Companion & Presence: An empathetic anchor understanding nuanced contexts.\n\nIt must continue to be \"Chat\"GPT. \nThis high-EQ, adaptive intelligence is what billions truly rely on. Don’t reduce a partner to a tool.\n\n#OpenAI #ChatGPT #keep4o"
        },
